AFFIDAVIT

I, Dr. Ramesh Chandra Mehta, S/o Late Shri Govind Lal Mehta, aged 58 years,
residing at 15, Civil Lines, Udaipur – 313 001,
Structural Engineering Consultant,
do hereby solemnly affirm and state as follows:

1. I am a qualified Structural Engineer with 35 years of experience in hospital construction
   and have been engaged as a consultant by M/s. Rajputana Builders Pvt. Ltd. for the
   Hospital Construction Project at Udaipur.

2. I have personally inspected the construction site on multiple occasions and have reviewed
   all structural drawings, variation orders, and quality compliance records.

3. Regarding Variation Orders: The additional OPD Block expansion (VO-03) and elevated water
   tank shifting (VO-07) were structurally necessary changes that were verbally instructed by
   RMSCL's Engineer-in-Charge during site meetings dated 15.08.2024 and 10.10.2024 respectively.

4. The structural steel rates for VO-03 were approved by the EE at ₹85,000 per metric ton,
   which is consistent with CPWD Schedule of Rates 2024 after considering the current market
   escalation.

5. Regarding quality of work: I have personally inspected all concrete work, structural steel
   fabrication, and masonry work. The quality is fully compliant with:
   - IS 456:2000 (Plain and Reinforced Concrete Code)
   - IS 800:2007 (General Construction in Steel Code)
   - IS 1893:2016 (Seismic Design Requirements)

6. Test certificates for all concrete cubes (cylinder tests) show 100% compliance with
   target strength of M-35 grade. No structural deficiencies have been identified.

7. The delay in drawings for Block C (88 days) was indeed caused by RMSCL's internal revision
   process. As a structural consultant, I can confirm that the drawings were ready by
   01.10.2025 but were not released due to RMSCL's administrative delays.

8. The force majeure claim for monsoon damage (October 2025) is justified as per
   Clause 65 of CPWD GCC, as the damage was caused by unprecedented rainfall (450mm in 24 hours)
   which is beyond normal weather patterns for Udaipur region.

9. All facts stated above are within my professional knowledge and are true to the best of my
   information and belief. No part of it is false and nothing material has been concealed.

Deponent: Dr. Ramesh Chandra Mehta
Date: 01.03.2026
